AB  - Convolutional neural networks are used to capture local features, but their limited receptive fields hinder the effective modeling of global semantics. On the other hand, Transformer-based models excel at capturing global features but lack the mining of detailed features. Our proposed method CTFuse combines the strengths of CNN and Transformer to enhance cloud detection performance. Specifically, We utilized the proposed Multi-scale Feature Pyramid Module (MS-FPM) and Multi-receptive-field Module (MRFM) to construct a CNN stream to capture a larger receptive field. To fully integrate the CNN stream and transformer stream, we carefully design the Information Injection Module (IIM). Furthermore, we enhance the decoder by incorporating skip-connection mechanisms that leverage low-level spatial context to restore high-level semantic pixel localizations, leading to precise cloud detection outcomes. Extensive experiments on SPARCS, GF1-WHU, and WHUS2-CD+ datasets demonstrate that the proposed CTFuse achieves superior cloud detection performance compared to most existing cloud detection techniques.
