AB  - Hyperspectral images (HSIs), with their high spectral and spatial resolution, offer great potential in classification tasks. However, high dimensionality and limited labeled data pose significant challenges, particularly in spectral–spatial features representation and model generalization. To address these challenges, we propose a novel model, HSCRN, which integrates 3D/2D convolutions for spectral–spatial representation and introduces two specialized modules: the FRRC module for adaptive refinement of discriminative features and the OCT module for dynamic context modeling across long-range dependencies. To validate the effectiveness of the proposed model, we conducted experiments on the Indian Pines (IP), Pavia University (PU), and Botswana (Bot) datasets. The experimental results demonstrate that our method achieves high classification accuracy and strong robustness, as evidenced by the overall accuracies (OAs) of 98.90 %, 98.81 %, and 97.39 % attained on the IP, PU, and Bot datasets, respectively. These findings advance the development of HSI technology and demonstrate significant application value in precision agriculture, environmental monitoring, and mineral exploration, among others.
