AB  - The Smart Fisheries App provides users with information regarding their fishing operations using many of the same features provided by other apps but in a single app instead of being spread out over many separate apps. This app allows users to have the most current information at their fingertips, locate the best possible route for fishing, and make wiser choices regarding fishing by utilising the collective data from many different sources. The Smart Fisheries App combines the use of various technologies such as IoT (Internet of Things), satellite imagery, cloud computing, and machine learning tools, in order to provide users with the ability to identify potential areas for productive fishing based on environmental variables (for example: water temperatures, salinity, chlorophyll concentration) to pinpoint where the highest concentrations of fish might be found. These environmental variables are analysed using predictive modelling algorithms that create heat maps for fishermen indicating where fish are most likely to be found, as well as providing route suggestions that proactively guide the users towards areas where f ish are believed to be plentiful while also factoring in an assessment of the user's environment to determine the best options for entering that area. The predictive models for fish presence are based upon the use of supervised machine learning techniques, such as Random Forest and Support Vector Machines, and provide reliable and easy to understand predictions based upon fish presence. Additionally, bio-inspired optimisation methods are being used in conjunction with the app, such as Genetic Algorithms (GA) and Ant Colony Optimisation (ACO) in order to generate optimal navigation routes that reduce overall distances travelled by users.
