AB  - This chapter introduces the design and application of Gabor wavelets in hyperspectral image (HSI) feature extraction and classification. Firstly, 2-D and 3-D Gabor wavelets are introduced for the feature extraction of spatial textures and spatial–spectral information, respectively. An improved fast-density peak-based clustering (FDPC) algorithm is implemented for further feature selection. Secondly, pixel-wise Gabor features are discussed for HSI classification, including prior optimization-based and deep-learning-based Gabor wavelets. A classification approach using 3-D Gabor wavelet-phase coding and Hamming distance matching (HDM) is illustrated. Thirdly, the integration of Gabor wavelets with superpixel segmentation is explored for HSI classification, along with the enhanced multiscale superpixel features. The methods of flexible Gabor (FG)-based superpixel-level unsupervised linear discriminant analysis (LDA) and cascade superpixel regularized Gabor feature fusion (CSRGFF) are demonstrated. Overall, the above spatial–spectral Gabor-based methods have the advantages of small sample learning and efficient classification in HSI classification tasks.
