AB  - To address the challenges of monitoring and predicting ground subsidence in mining areas, this study proposes an integrated approach combining Persistent Scatterer Interferometric Synthetic Aperture Radar technology with the Dung Beetle Optimizer-Long Short-Term Memory model, using the Zixing Mining Area in Hunan Province as a case study. Using 66 ascending-track Sentinel-1A satellite images, PS-InSAR technology was employed to obtain high-precision time-series subsidence data from 2020 to 2023. The subsidence rate increased from -5.98mm yr to -16.08mm yr during the observation period. Based on building tilt rate indicators, four buildings were classified as Risk Level II (unstable), and one was classified as risk level III(requiring attention). Settlement trend predictions will be conducted for buildings with risk levels greater than II. To enhance measurement accuracy, we harnessed DBO to optimize LSTM hyperparameters, yielding the DBO-LSTM architecture. Comparative experiments reveal that the DBO-LSTM model exhibits superior performance over alternative optimizationbased LSTM variants. The predicted settlement curves align most closely with actual measured values. This study provides an accurate and intelligent technical solution for structural subsidence surveillance and forecast in subsurface extraction zones.
