AB  - Built-up is a key land use class representing impervious surfaces and reflecting regional development. Analysing built-up growth helps understand urban expansion and supports sustainable planning. This study utilises multi-spectral optical satellite data with an indices-based approach and a Dense Neural Network (DNN) model to extract built-up areas, which are further refined using nighttime light data. Multi-temporal data spanning 35 years at 5 -year intervals is analysed for Hyderabad and its surroundings. Google Earth Engine and Google Colab are integrated to leverage cloud resources for data processing and deep learning with 98% model accuracy. The extracted built-up layers are validated using 400 reference points, achieving an accuracy of 85-90%. Two spatio-temporal methods, radial graph analysis and Shannon's relative entropy, are used to assess the nature and pattern of urban growth over time.
