AB  - The work is devoted to the problem of mine detection using copter-type unmanned aerial vehicles. The work considers several stages of the process: gathering information, orthophotomosaic restoration, and intelligent data processing for the purpose of detecting mines. Two algorithms are proposed for constructing reference points for search zones that are bound by a convex polygon. Experiments were conducted using the proposed methods with multispectral and thermal cameras. The quality of the received individual images, the quality of the reconstructed orthophotomosaic, and the accuracy of their processing by intelligent systems were analyzed. The proposed algorithms are capable of successfully calculating reference points that can be used to construct an orthophotomosaic, which enables the detection of explosive objects with a diameter of 0.1 meters or more using artificial intelligence-based explosive detection systems.
